{
  "id": "fluency-l6-gauss",
  "lesson": "l6-gauss",
  "title": "Fluency: arithmetic series",
  "n": 20,
  "pass": 0.9,
  "minutes": 10,
  "families": [
    {
      "id": "one-to-n",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "add the whole numbers from 1",
      "vars": { "m": { "int": [10, 200] } },
      "let": { "mp": "m + 1", "mm": "m - 1", "sum": "m*(m + 1)/2", "whole": "m*(m + 1)", "short": "m*(m - 1)/2" },
      "prompt": "What is $1 + 2 + 3 + \\dots + {m}$?",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{sum}", "tol": { "abs": 0 }, "placeholder": "A whole number" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "not-halved", "value": "{whole}", "line": "You added the sum forwards and backwards. That counts every term twice, so halve it." },
        { "id": "one-term-short", "value": "{short}", "line": "You worked out $\\dfrac{{{m} \\times {mm}}}{{2}}$. Each pair is $1 + {m} = {mp}$, not {mm}." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Pair the first term with the last: each pair is $1 + {m} = {mp}$.",
        "Forwards plus backwards makes {m} columns of {mp}, so the sum is $\\dfrac{{{m} \\times {mp}}}{{2}} = {sum}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "first-n-terms",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "sum the first n terms of an arithmetic series",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [-10, 20], "not": [0] },
        "d": { "int": [-6, 9], "not": [0] },
        "k": { "int": [8, 30] }
      },
      "let": {
        "t2": "a + d", "t3": "a + 2*d", "km": "k - 1",
        "inner": "2*a + (k - 1)*d", "sum": "k*(2*a + (k - 1)*d)/2",
        "whole": "k*(2*a + (k - 1)*d)", "kd": "k*(2*a + k*d)/2"
      },
      "where": ["sum != 0", "t2 != 0", "t3 != 0"],
      "prompt": "Find the sum of the first {k} terms of ${a}{t2:+}{t3:+} + \\dots$",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{sum}", "tol": { "abs": 0 }, "placeholder": "A whole number" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "not-halved", "value": "{whole}", "line": "You forgot to halve. Forwards plus backwards counts the sum twice." },
        { "id": "k-steps", "value": "{kd}", "line": "You used {k} steps of $d$. The last of {k} terms is only {km} steps after the first." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Here $a = {a}$, $d = {t2} - {a:()} = {d}$ and $n = {k}$.",
        "$2a + (n - 1)d = 2 \\times {a:()} + {km} \\times {d:()} = {inner}$.",
        "So $S_{{{k}}} = \\dfrac{{{k}}}{{2}} \\times {inner:()} = {sum}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "up-to-last-term",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "count the terms, then sum",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [1, 30] },
        "d": { "int": [-5, 9], "not": [0] },
        "k": { "int": [8, 40] }
      },
      "let": {
        "t2": "a + d", "t3": "a + 2*d", "l": "a + (k - 1)*d", "km": "k - 1",
        "al": "2*a + (k - 1)*d", "sum": "k*(2*a + (k - 1)*d)/2",
        "steps": "(k - 1)*(2*a + (k - 1)*d)/2", "whole": "k*(2*a + (k - 1)*d)"
      },
      "where": ["l > 0"],
      "prompt": "What is ${a}{t2:+}{t3:+} + \\dots {l:+}$?",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{sum}", "tol": { "abs": 0 }, "placeholder": "A whole number" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "counted-steps", "value": "{steps}", "line": "You used {km} terms, which is the number of steps. There are {k} terms, one more than the steps." },
        { "id": "not-halved", "value": "{whole}", "line": "You forgot to halve. Forwards plus backwards counts the sum twice." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "The step is {d}, so there are $({l} - {a}) \\div {d:()} + 1 = {k}$ terms.",
        "Pair the first term with the last: each pair is ${a} + {l:()} = {al}$.",
        "So the sum is $\\dfrac{{{k} \\times {al:()}}}{{2}} = {sum}$."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
